{"seq": 22, "agent": "comms", "agent_role": "comms", "server": "tickets", "tool": "save_postmortem", "kind": "write", "args": {"incident_id": "ui-CheckoutErrorRateHigh-20261107T122953Z", "postmortem": {"summary": "At ~2026-11-07T12:21:44 a feature flag 'paymentFailure' was rolled to 50%, after which the payment service's server-span error fraction rose and sampled traces showed repeated 'Invalid token' failures that caused checkout PlaceOrder errors. Triage and diagnosis supported the hypothesis that the flag rollout caused payment failures. The mitigation was to set the 'paymentFailure' flag to off (approved and executed), after which verification showed the checkout error rate recovered to 0.0; final status: recovered.", "root_cause": "Feature flag 'paymentFailure' was rolled to 50% and injected payment failures (invalid token) in the payment service, producing a large increase in payment errors that propagated to checkout.", "action": {"tool": "set_flag", "flag": "paymentFailure", "variant": "off"}, "timeline": [{"at": "2026-11-07T12:30:04.675541Z", "node": "intake", "kind": "plan", "text": "Alert CheckoutErrorRateHigh on checkout: Checkout error rate above 5% for 5 minutes"}, {"at": "2026-11-07T12:30:11.761578Z", "node": "commander_plan", "kind": "plan", "text": "Plan v1: scope \u2192 hypotheses \u2192 test \u2192 act \u2192 verify \u2192 communicate"}, {"at": "2026-11-07T12:30:34.664179Z", "node": "triage", "kind": "triage", "text": "SEV1 (S1.1); suspects checkout, payment, email; Customers are failing to complete purchases \u2014 checkout is returning errors and is slow, likely due to failing payments."}, {"at": "2026-11-07T12:30:39.811468Z", "node": "commander_hypothesize", "kind": "plan", "text": "Testing: payment/paymentFailure"}, {"at": "2026-11-07T12:31:20.332567Z", "node": "diagnosis", "kind": "verdict", "text": "payment/paymentFailure: supported (4 calls) \u2014 Temporal correlation between the flag rollout and rising payment error rate plus multiple traces that show identical 'Invalid token' payment failures during checkout. Signals are independent (feature flag change, metrics, and traces) and align on the same failure mode and time window."}, {"at": "2026-11-07T12:31:24.476702Z", "node": "commander_assess", "kind": "verdict", "text": "converge: payment/paymentFailure supported"}, {"at": "2026-11-07T12:31:40.861630Z", "node": "runbook", "kind": "verdict", "text": "runbook RB-001; lessons applicable [], rejected []"}, {"at": "2026-11-07T12:31:48.181040Z", "node": "propose_action", "kind": "action", "text": "Proposed {\"tool\":\"set_flag\",\"flag\":\"paymentFailure\",\"variant\":\"off\"}"}, {"at": "2026-11-07T12:31:49.736047Z", "node": "dry_run", "kind": "action", "text": "Dry run: set flag paymentFailure from 50% to off"}, {"at": "2026-11-07T12:31:49.902503Z", "node": "approval_gate", "kind": "approval", "text": "approve by uppili: live hooks check: turns off the injected fault"}, {"at": "2026-11-07T12:31:51.898666Z", "node": "execute", "kind": "action", "text": "Executed: set flag paymentFailure to off"}, {"at": "2026-11-07T12:35:11.815951Z", "node": "verify", "kind": "verdict", "text": "recovered: checkout error_rate since fix = 0.0 (0.0/7.067137809187279 requests) (threshold 0.05)"}], "lessons_proposed": [{"text": "Gate feature-flag rollouts with short canaries and an automated abort if the payment error fraction rises above an acceptable threshold (e.g., 5% over 5m).", "service": "payment", "fault_family": "paymentFailure", "preconditions": [{"check": "recent_change", "args": {"flag": "paymentFailure", "within": "15m"}}, {"check": "promql_above", "args": {"query": "(sum(rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{service_name=\"payment\",span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_SERVER\",status_code=\"STATUS_CODE_ERROR\"}[5m])) or vector(0)) / sum(rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{service_name=\"payment\",span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_SERVER\"}[5m]))", "threshold": 0.05}}]}, {"text": "Add an automated flag rollback (circuit-breaker) that pauses or rolls back rollouts when associated downstream services show sudden error-rate increases, and ensure rollouts are annotated in alerts/runbooks for faster triage.", "service": "payment", "fault_family": "paymentFailure", "preconditions": [{"check": "recent_change", "args": {"flag": "paymentFailure", "within": "30m"}}, {"check": "promql_above", "args": {"query": "(sum(rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{service_name=\"checkout\",span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_SERVER\",status_code=\"STATUS_CODE_ERROR\"}[5m])) or vector(0)) / sum(rate(traces_span_metrics_calls_total{service_name=\"checkout\",span_kind=\"SPAN_KIND_SERVER\"}[5m]))", "threshold": 0.05}}]}]}}, "payload_hash": null, "ok": true, "blocked": false, "block_reason": null, "action_id": null, "purpose": null, "driver": "code", "args_hash": "545415296969b465", "latency_ms": 1858, "result_size": 57}
